    "narrative": "The LawDog offense is primed for a high-ceiling performance against Patrick Corbin today, with **Taylor Ward** headlining our active roster as the strongest play of the day with a 71.19 score. Batting lead-off, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against the struggling Corbin; his ability to set the table is critical to our Roto efficiency. **Daulton Varsho** also provides a high-floor start (69.94) hitting third against Chris Bassitt. While Bassitt is a more competent arm than Corbin, **Daulton Varsho**\u2019s platoon edge and high-leverage lineup spot mitigate the threat, though we are monitoring the \"Elite Hold\" risk, as Bassitt's profile could limit the stolen base opportunities we desperately need to chase.\n\n**Jeremiah Jackson** rounds out the active trio at 56.35, though he remains a marginal play largely tethered to his assumed #9 spot in the order. His score is bolstered by the weak opposing SP_xERA, but the volatility of the bottom-of-the-order hitting makes him a \"start with caution\" candidate. Looking at our bench, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Lawrence Butler** were held out due to team off-days, while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains unavailable for the same reason. The absence of **Cal Raleigh** due to his IL designation continues to compress our depth, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining core of **Tyler Freeman**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Masyn Winn** for secondary production. We are closely monitoring lineup confirmations for **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Taylor Ward**, and **Daulton Varsho**, as any defensive alignment shifts that drop them further down the order would significantly impact their projected output and force a re-evaluation of our daily cap preservation strategy.",
